| `secrets.scanner.refused_files` | list of strings | `[".gitleaks.toml", ".gitleaksignore"]` | a non-empty list of bare file names, no `/` or `\` | `scripts/scan_secrets.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.refused_files` row | Names the scanner's own config and ignore files: a scan refuses to run, exit 14, while git would commit one anywhere in the tree or one exists at the root, because such a file decides what the scan judges. Removing a name lets that file silence findings. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.refused_files = [".gitleaks.toml", ".gitleaksignore"]` to stderr. | excusing a finding: `secrets.scanner.exclusions` | always |
